Z||000000||MotherGoose||05-08-2000||12:34 PM||||Also My door ajar light is always on.  whats up there?||||reg||5
Z||000001||deceler8||05-08-2000||01:24 PM||||Well, there's only four places to check for this problem...<P>I believe the "ajar" light only comes on when a circuit is completed...when door/trunk/hood is open, the circuit is completed. So this should be fairly easy to figure out...usually one of the pinswitches "freezes" open or shut.<P>Try pulling/pushing on the switches to see if they move freely. Pay special attention to the hood switch and be sure the trunk switch isn't broken (the plastic tab that opens the switch can break off).<P>If you can't fix the problem, you can always take the bulb out of the "ajar" socket on the inst. panel.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierosound||05-09-2000||12:08 AM||||Check the pin switch for the front hood.  Because they sit vertically, water manages to get in there.  It's probably rusted and shorted out.  I've replaced this every couple of years, so I keep an extra on hand.||||reg||1
